fact WorkItem(id: "WI-672", description: some(value: "GOAL (design direction, user 2026-07-10 'eventually we should have no short-name as key'): eliminate SHORT-NAME index keys and key the reflect-fact indexes by CANONICAL IDENTITY instead. Two live short-name keys: SortInfoIndex.by_name (WI-673) and ProvidesIndex.by_carrier (WI-660). Both are forced by same_symbol's BRIDGE #2 (a bare short name matches the last segment of a qualified name), which canonical_sort_sym cannot reproduce (its doc caveat: a bare/short symbol has no by_qualified_name entry -> falls to identity; divergences must be fixed at the PRODUCER). ROOT CAUSE (traced this session via probes): namespace-less TOP-LEVEL declarations land in the _global scope with a BARE qualified name (QN == short name, no dot) -- loader current_scope defaults to _global (load.rs:1214/995) and only switches on a  decl (load.rs:1254). When such a bare _global sort coincides by short name with a qualified stdlib sort (e.g. a testcase's top-level / in anthill-testcases/ring-polynom/*.anthill loaded ALONGSIDE the stdlib's anthill.prelude.List / anthill.prelude.algebra.Ring), same_symbol bridge #2 CONFLATES the two DISTINCT sorts, and find_sort_info returns the prelude sort's ctors/ops for the testcase's sort. PROBE EVIDENCE: find_sort_info received bare List/Option/Pair/Ring, all kind=RESOLVED scope=_global (NOT unresolved -- the NotFound->intern-bare fallback at load.rs:6372 fired 0 times), matching qualified anthill.prelude.* via bridge #2; the full-stdlib CLI load (all sorts qualified) was clean. So it is NOT an unresolved-name or type-info-deferral issue -- it is bare _global QNs colliding with qualified stdlib QNs. FIX OPTIONS (STOP-AND-ASK -- touches loader name-resolution / language scoping): (a) AUTO-QUALIFY _global/top-level declarations so their QN carries a dot (e.g.  or file/module-rooted) -> same_symbol bridge #2 (which requires one side to be truly bare, no dot) can no longer fire -> DROP bridge #2 and key SortInfo/by_carrier by canonical_sort_sym like ProvidesIndex.by_spec_base; (b) mandate namespaces (breaking, biggest); (c) narrowest stopgap: give the colliding testcases a  (one line each) so their sorts stop colliding -- but that does not remove the general mechanism. CAVEAT: _global is not only user-convenience -- it also anchors kernel-vocab/reflect resolution (resolve_name_in_global, the prelude_qualified lowest-precedence fallback), so the lever is 'stop top-level user decls producing bare QNs that collide with stdlib', NOT 'delete _global'. Acceptance: same_symbol bridge #2 provably never fires (or is removed); SortInfoIndex + ProvidesIndex re-keyed by canonical_sort_sym with a DEBUG cross-check (bucket must contain every same_symbol-matching fact, so a future bare query is a LOUD test failure not a silent empty result); full suite green; behaviour verified unchanged (or the de-conflation is intentional + tests updated). WI-661 bucket-1 tail; the concrete form of the umbrella's 'canonicalize query symbols at producers' lever."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "user", at: "2026-07-11T03:31:35Z"))

fact Tag(workitem: "WI-672", name: "carrier-agnostic")

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-672", author: "user", content: "CORE (user 2026-07-10, emphatic): comparison by SHORT-NAME (last qualified-name segment) must be ELIMINATED from the KB -- the index keys AND the same_symbol BRIDGE #2 they rest on. (The auto-added description above lost a few literal words to shell escaping -- the substance is: same_symbol bridge #2 = a bare short name matching the last segment of a qualified name; it exists only because namespace-less top-level decls get bare _global QNs that collide with qualified stdlib QNs by last segment. Fix at the PRODUCER so no bare colliding QNs exist, then delete bridge #2 and key SortInfoIndex/ProvidesIndex by canonical_sort_sym.) Ticket count does not matter; the invariant does: no short-name/last-segment matching. See memory no-short-name-comparison. Marked in-code at SortInfoIndex struct doc (typing.rs).", at: "2026-07-10T09:21:35Z")
